.TH tuimage n 0.2 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tuimage
.PP
Pure\-Tcl image \fBinspection\fR: detect format, MIME type and pixel dimensions from an image's raw bytes, plus \fBdata:\fR URI helpers. It does \fBno\fR decoding or pixel processing \-\- that belongs to Tk's photo images or the \fBimgtools\fR extension. Reuses \fBtclutils::tubase64\fR.
.SS API
.CS
tuimage::type $bytes          ;# png | jpeg | gif | bmp | webp | ""
tuimage::mime $bytes          ;# image/png ...
tuimage::dimensions $bytes    ;# {width height}  (or {} if unknown)
tuimage::inspect $bytes       ;# {type .. mime .. width .. height ..}
tuimage::dataUri image/png $bytes   ;# -> "data:image/png;base64,...."
tuimage::fromDataUri $uri           ;# -> {mime image/png bytes <raw>}
.CE
.PP
\fBfromDataUri\fR splits the parameters at \fB;\fR outside double quotes: in \fBcharset="utf\-8;base64"\fR the \fBbase64\fR belongs to the value and does not switch on decoding (0.2).
.PP
Dimensions are read straight from the header (PNG IHDR, GIF screen descriptor, BMP info header, JPEG SOFn scan, WEBP VP8/VP8L/VP8X). \fB$bytes\fR must be raw binary (e.g. a file read from a binary channel, or \fBtubase64::decode\fR of an embedded photo). Useful for vCard/CalDAV photos, thumbnails and validation without loading a full image toolkit.
